  "body": "## What happens\n\nOn a tool change, `assets/posts/heidenhain.cps:381-392` writes only `T<n> G17 S..` and then `M3`. It writes no retract, no `M6` and no `M0`. The next block is `G00 G40 G90 Z+<clearance>` with the length of the **new** tool.\n\nThe engine does not refuse this. `crates/post/src/post/machine_installation.rs:67-68` only passes `toolChangeMode` to the script, and the DIN/ISO post never reads it.\n\n## Why it is wrong on the Fehlmann Picomax 55 (iTNC 530, NC 340490-03)\n\n- The machine has a manual tool change (`assets/machines/fehlmann-picomax55.mch`).\n- The machine's programming manual changes a tool with `L Z+0 R0 FMAX M92`, then an XY park move with `M6`. TOOL CALL comes before the M6 move (manual p. 2-11 and p. 2-19).\n- The machine parameters from the delivery CD (the machine parameter file) confirm it:\n  - MP 7440 bit 0 = 0: the program halts at M06.\n  - MP 7480.0 = 1: TOOL CALL only passes the T number to the PLC. TOOL CALL does not stop the program.\n  - MP 950 / MP 4210.0: the tool-change height is M92 Z-0.05.\n\nA multi-tool DIN/ISO program therefore runs on with the old tool in the spindle, and the new tool's length and speed are active. This gives a wrong Z and a possible crash.\n\nThe machine file selects the Klartext post, which stops with `M0`. The defect occurs when a user selects the DIN/ISO post for a manual-change machine.\n\n## Expected\n\nOne of:\n- The DIN/ISO post refuses by name when `toolChangeMode` is a manual mode; or\n- it writes the manual change sequence: retract `G00 G90 Z+0 M92` (or the machine file's change position), then `M6` (a stop by MP 7440 on this machine).\n\nAlso add an engine law: a post that does not handle `toolChangeMode` is refused on a manual-change machine, so other posts cannot have the same defect.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A two-tool job on the Picomax machine with the DIN/ISO post either refuses by name or writes a retract and a stop before the second tool cuts.\n- A test pins this. Automatic-change machines are unchanged (goldens byte-identical).\n\nSource: review of the posts against the Picomax 55 programming manual and its machine parameters. Related: #3095.",
